<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>How do I simplify a fraction?</h3>
    <p>Find the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) of the numerator and denominator, then divide both by it. For example, 24/36 has GCD 12. Dividing both by 12 gives 2/3, which is the fully simplified form. The calculator does this automatically for every result.</p>

    <h3>What is a mixed fraction?</h3>
    <p>A mixed fraction combines a whole number with a proper fraction, like 2 and 3/4. To use mixed fractions in this calculator enter the whole number in the first field and the fraction parts in the numerator and denominator fields. The calculator converts to improper fractions internally for accuracy.</p>

    <h3>What is the LCD and why do I need it for adding fractions?</h3>
    <p>LCD stands for Least Common Denominator. Fractions can only be added or subtracted if they reference the same-sized parts. The LCD is the smallest number that both denominators divide into evenly. Converting both fractions to use the LCD makes the addition or subtraction straightforward.</p>

    <h3>Can I use this to solve homework problems step by step?</h3>
    <p>Yes. The step display shows each stage of the calculation the same way a textbook would. You can use the steps to check your own work or to understand where you made an error.</p>
</section>

